    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract ideas and practical problem-solving—something I find both challenging and deeply rewarding. My parents’ education levels made it harder to access structured learning early, but my curiosity for patterns in art and philosophy pushed me toward exploring its logic. It’s not just numbers; it’s the language of existence itself.",
